WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.160
"John Wick: Chapter 4" was a definitive finale for&nbsp;
the film series in more ways than one, but that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.400
doesn't mean there aren't a few windows still&nbsp;
open that John could leap through at any time.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.600
John Wick duels with Caine during the epic&nbsp;
conclusion of "John Wick: Chapter 4." And while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.620
the hitman conspires to trick and ultimately&nbsp;
defeat the film's real villain, the Marquis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:21.240
de Gramont, Wick succumbs to his wounds. However,&nbsp;
after the heartbreaking last moments of the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.620
there's a post-credits scene between Caine&nbsp;
and Akira that alludes to a possible spin-off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.300
but without the franchise's main character.&nbsp;
While producer Erica Lee seems to insist that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.980
audiences should accept John Wick's tombstone at&nbsp;
face value, she's also not one to count the Baba&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:39.420
Yaga out. During an interview with "Collider,"&nbsp;
Lee asked and answered her own question, saying,

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.220
"I think that... is that character of John&nbsp;
Wick dead? Yes. Are there other versions or...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.720
I don't know, I never say never. It's a long&nbsp;
life. We're developing other properties, too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.740
and I think that there's a lot of opportunity&nbsp;
for movies starring other characters or other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.920
ways to worldbuild movies that are sort&nbsp;
of handovers to different characters."

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.180
Indeed, Wick might have perished during his&nbsp;
climactic battle at sunrise, but there's another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.080
heavy hitter involved in the fight: the box&nbsp;
office. Within days of the movie's release,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:09.540
"John Wick: Chapter 4" had already made over $150&nbsp;
million worldwide. And the latest installment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.860
continues to win over both critics and audiences.&nbsp;
So, given all the spin-offs in development,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.060
don't be surprised if Reeves returns in&nbsp;
the future, even if it's just as a cameo.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:26.280
"The only way John Wick will ever&nbsp;
have freedom and peace, is in death."

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.940
Even though John Wick is dead, the&nbsp;
franchise is moving forward. First up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.480
there's the television mini-series "The&nbsp;
Continental." That will be followed by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:38.220
feature film titled "Ballerina." Interestingly,&nbsp;
taking a look at "Ballerina's" credits on IMDb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.660
Keanu Reeves is listed as a cast member. Because&nbsp;
the movie takes place between the third and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.380
fourth films, it's reasonable to believe&nbsp;
that John Wick could show up in the Ana de&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.700
Armas-led project. Erica Lee further cemented the&nbsp;
connection between the two films when she said,

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:54.780
"Making 'Ballerina' has actually been a really&nbsp;
interesting process because it's a lot of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.140
stuff that we take from the 'John Wick'&nbsp;
movies. But then it's slightly different.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:02.040
It's been fun to work on 'John Wick 4'&nbsp;
and 'Ballerina' kind of simultaneously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.180
and the TV show ['The Continental'], it's a lot&nbsp;
of Wick, but a lot of different versions of it."

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:10.380
Erica Lee isn't the only "John Wick: Chapter&nbsp;
4" producer leaving the door open for more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:14.700
Keanu Reeves in the franchise's future.&nbsp;
Producer Basil Iwanyck spoke to IndieWire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.820
about the film's final moments and what&nbsp;
it could mean for the character's future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:21.540
stating, "It's an ambiguous ending."&nbsp;
Seeing John Wick's grave certainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:25.800
leaves an emotional impact no one would want&nbsp;
to diminish, and it's clear if Wick's going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.620
to return to this world of violence,&nbsp;
it has to be done in the right way.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:32.760
After all, the movie shows Wick collapsing on&nbsp;
a staircase before cutting away to his grave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.900
in a cemetery. A lot could've happened between&nbsp;
those two scenes, so there's room for Wick to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:40.500
still be alive out there somewhere. Iwanyck&nbsp;
confirms that ambiguity was intentional:

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.780
"I don't think we've boxed&nbsp;
ourselves into any corner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:44.820
whether he's dead or alive,&nbsp;
at the end of this movie."

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:48.120
With so many spinoffs in the works, you&nbsp;
better believe that if those pulling the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:52.080
strings think they can make bank by bringing&nbsp;
Keanu Reeves back, they'll do everything they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.740
can to convince the star to put on his&nbsp;
kevlar-lined suit jacket one more time.

